---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import licences from '../../THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md?raw';
---

<Base
  title="About ForeverQR: credits and licences"
  description="Who made ForeverQR, why it exists, and the open-source libraries and fonts it ships with, each with its licence."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">About ForeverQR</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-lg">A free QR code studio that makes codes that never expire, and a checker that tells you whether someone else's code will.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">Why it exists</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
      Many QR code sites sell "dynamic" codes: the code points at their server, and when the subscription ends the code stops
      working. ForeverQR makes static codes that hold your content directly, so there is nothing to renew and nothing to
      switch off. It runs entirely in your browser, with no accounts and no tracking. The{' '}
      <a href="/privacy/" class="underline underline-offset-2">privacy page</a> explains what runs where.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">Credits</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
      Built by Arpan Mandal with Astro, Svelte and Tailwind CSS. QR encoding by qrcode-generator, QR reading by zxing-wasm
      (a WebAssembly build of zxing-cpp), PDF export by pdf-lib. Fonts are Inter and Archivo Black, both under the SIL Open
      Font License. The source link will be added here once the repository is public.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">Licences</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">The complete list of third-party code and fonts shipped with the site, verbatim:</p>
    <pre
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="Third-party licences"
      class="mt-3 max-h-[32rem] overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-4 text-xs leading-5 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">{licences.replaceAll('`', '')}</pre>
  </div>
</Base>
